\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Swap interventions. \emph  {Top:} intervention diagrams with measured supernode readouts (grey percentages; ``pinned'' = at or below the patch end layer $\ell $, clamped by the protocol); badges give the paper's steering multiples. \emph  {Bottom:} strength ladders, $P(\text  {expected answer})$ vs.\ donor multiple $s$, with the paper endpoint dotted. Left: the operation swap under the constrained protocol (solid, flat) vs.\ the live-attention probe (dashed) --- the QK-mediated channel. Middle: the operand swap crosses in all six configurations (dots mark crossovers; raw-zh at $18\times $). Right: the language swap peaks near the paper's own $6\times $ and saturates; fr$\to $en's curve tracks ``large'' while the actual output is the paper's token ``big'' ($0.753$ at $6\times $).}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ml-interv}{{3}{8}{Swap interventions. \emph {Top:} intervention diagrams with measured supernode readouts (grey percentages; ``pinned'' = at or below the patch end layer $\ell $, clamped by the protocol); badges give the paper's steering multiples. \emph {Bottom:} strength ladders, $P(\text {expected answer})$ vs.\ donor multiple $s$, with the paper endpoint dotted. Left: the operation swap under the constrained protocol (solid, flat) vs.\ the live-attention probe (dashed) --- the QK-mediated channel. Middle: the operand swap crosses in all six configurations (dots mark crossovers; raw-zh at $18\times $). Right: the language swap peaks near the paper's own $6\times $ and saturates; fr$\to $en's curve tracks ``large'' while the actual output is the paper's token ``big'' ($0.753$ at $6\times $)}{figure.3}{}}
